oxygen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of carbon. Given that the atomic masses of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>, respectively. The data agrees with how many formulae of the following?</p><p>A.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></math></p><p>B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCHO</mi></math></p><p>C.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>OOCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>D.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3f4b17", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80d7"}, {"id": "a0230c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80d8"}, {"id": "6577d4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80d9"}, {"id": "5ed12b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80da"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80db", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df92"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477f"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b60"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.<