0e2"}, {"id": "a45cb2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80e3"}, {"id": "a93041", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80e4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80e5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df92"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477f"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b60"], "question": {"text": "When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> nitric acid is heated in a beaker, its volume is reduced to half and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of nitric acid is evaporated. The molarity of the remaining nitric acid solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>. (Molar mass of nitric acid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>63</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "31a824", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80e6"}, {"id": "824b96", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80e7"}, {"id": "ca72d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80e8"}, {"id": "ea90d1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80e9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80ea", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df92"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b75"], "concepts": ["6176f3f86581241c7072b276"], "question": {"text": "The volume of hydrogen liberated at STP by treating&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;of magnesium with excess of hydrochloric acid is ......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>. Given Molar volume of gas is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>&nbsp;at STP. Molar mass of magnesium is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "33c44a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80eb"}, {"id": "5fa67f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80ec"}, {"id": "346867", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80ed"}, {"id": "a93f51", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80ee"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80ef", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df92"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477f"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b60"], "question": {"text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>50</mn></math> molal solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KOH</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>aq</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;has a density of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>89</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The molarity of the solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p><p>[Atomic masses: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>39</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "662db1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f0"}, {"id": "0fbd85", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f1"}, {"id": "f0b9d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f2"}, {"id": "7e4a34", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df92"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b75"], "concepts": ["6162fb716ed13040ec84ef69"], "question": {"text": "Complete combustion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>750</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of an organic compound provides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>420</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>210</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. The percentage composition of carbon and hydrogen in organic compound is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and ______ respectively. (Round off to the Nearest Integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "f330b6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f5"}, {"id": "62e669", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f6"}, {"id": "f4af5e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f7"}, {"id": "64cc3d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80f9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df92"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b75"], "concepts": ["6162fb716ed13040ec84ef5c"], "question": {"text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff479d491-e048-4d8f-8e2b-b0295bcda028-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 167px; height: 120px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>In the above reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of toluene is converted into benzaldehyde with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>92</mn><mo>%</mo></math> yield. The amount of benzaldehyde produced is____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "be2dae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80fa"}, {"id": "9d60a8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80fb"}, {"id": "600f03", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80fc"}, {"id": "f19f20", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efcc677dc36a88f80fd"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "m